    "result_text": "All 279 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented digits-only telephone storage with normalization applied before the uniqueness check.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Relaxed the `telephone` validation pattern from `^[0-9]*$` to `^[0-9 ()-]*$` so formatted numbers like `(613) 555-0100` pass request-body bean validation (which runs before the controller executes) instead of being rejected with a 400. The generated `OwnerFieldsDto` is rebuilt from this spec at compile time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**:\n   - Added a `normalizeTelephone` helper that strips spaces, dashes and parentheses (`replaceAll(\"[\\\\s()-]\", \"\")`), leaving digits only (null-safe).\n   - In `addOwner`, normalize the telephone immediately after mapping \u2014 **before** the `isDuplicateOwner` uniqueness check and before saving \u2014 so `(613) 555-0100` and `6135550100` collide as the same number, and the stored/returned value is digits-only.\n   - In `updateOwner`, applied the same normalization when setting the telephone, keeping stored data consistent.\n\nThe normalized value (`6135550100`, 10 digits) also satisfies the existing `Owner` entity's `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{10}$\")` constraint at persist time.\n\n**Verification:** Full suite green \u2014 279 tests, 0 failures. The new `Cp11Tests` (`coreStoresDigitsOnly`, `functionalityNormalisedDuplicateRejected`) both pass, and no existing tests regressed.",
